// Fyne platform package.
//
// Three `#[intrinsic]` primitives — Widget, Container, Wrapper — are the whole
// of what this platform's Go emitter knows how to build. Which Fyne widget one
// of them becomes is *data*: a `Spec` record, passed as a prop, naming the Go
// constructor to call, the Go type it returns, the import paths those two
// spellings need, and the setter or callback field behind each value it can be
// given. `spec.go` decodes that record; nothing in the Go emitter names a Fyne
// type or a component.
//
// The three primitives differ only in their children contract, because that is
// what a component declaration cannot express as data:
//
//   Widget     no children      — a leaf.
//   Container  a rest slot           — children attach through a method (`Add`).
//   Wrapper    component        — the child is assigned to a field (`Content`).
//
// Everything in fyne.sngl past Widget/Container/Wrapper — Label, Button, VBox and the rest
// — is an ordinary component declaration carrying a Spec, and so is anything a
// user writes. Wrapping a Fyne widget this package never heard of, from a Go
// module that is not Fyne's, is writing one more of them: `Spec.imports` is
// where the import path comes from, so no Go table has to grow a row.
//
// Value props:
//   A prop's *value* has to reach the emitter through a declared prop, because
//   that is what lowering turns into the `node.prop = expr` assignment the
//   emitter sees. The primitives therefore declare a small vocabulary of value
//   props by type — text, placeholder, number, flag, options — and `Setter`
//   binds one of them to a Go method. The vocabulary grows with the *types* a
//   Fyne setter takes, not with the widget count.
//
// Events:
//   Likewise: `@click`, `@change` and `@input` are the declared events, and
//   `Handler` binds one to a Go callback field, its Go func signature, and the
//   name of the parameter carrying the value (so a two-way `:value` bind can
//   read it straight off the callback rather than off an event struct Fyne
//   never passes).
//
// Style:
//   Every widget takes a `style` so an override can forward the stdlib
//   component's through, but no Spec in fyne.sngl gives it a setter — Fyne has no
//   style surface these constructors reach. The prop carries the data a future
//   theme/layout implementation needs; today the assignment is dropped.
